sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Payer as Originator<br/>(Harbor Properties)
    participant SB as Sending Bank<br/>(JPMorgan Chase)
    participant Fed as Federal Reserve<br/>Fedwire Funds Service
    participant RB as Receiving Bank<br/>(Bank of America)
    participant Payee as Beneficiary<br/>(Northside Title)

    Payer->>SB: Wire instruction, 4,200,000 USD<br/>Routing, account, beneficiary name

    SB->>SB: Dual authorization check
    SB->>Payer: Callback verification to a known number
    Payer-->>SB: Confirmed
    SB->>SB: OFAC screening, fraud rules,<br/>funds or intraday line check

    Note over SB,Fed: Last point at which the payment<br/>can be stopped unilaterally

    SB->>Fed: pacs.008 customer credit transfer<br/>over FedLine Direct

    Fed->>Fed: Validate message structure,<br/>sender authority, receiver RTN
    Fed->>Fed: Check sending bank master account

    alt Sufficient balance or daylight overdraft capacity
        Fed->>Fed: DEBIT sender master account 4,200,000<br/>CREDIT receiver master account 4,200,000<br/>(same transaction, central bank money)
        Fed-->>SB: Acknowledgement with IMAD
        Fed->>RB: Deliver message with OMAD
        Note over Fed,RB: Payment is now FINAL and IRREVOCABLE<br/>under Reg J and UCC 4A
    else Cap exhausted, no balance
        Fed-->>SB: Reject or queue per sender configuration
    end

    RB->>RB: OFAC screening on receipt
    RB->>Payee: Credit beneficiary account<br/>Available by close of the funds transfer day

    Note over Payer,Payee: Elapsed time: seconds.<br/>The callback in step 3 is the slow part, deliberately.

    alt Payer discovers fraud afterwards
        Payer->>SB: Request recall
        SB->>Fed: Send request for return (camt.056)
        Fed->>RB: Deliver request
        RB->>RB: Return is voluntary.<br/>Nothing compels the money back.
    end
